ere</div><div class="text-color-secondary">coverage and comms become</div></div></div><div>Low Earth Orbit is well suited for missions that rely on proximity to Earth. With K2’s high-power platforms and advanced propulsion systems, LEO becomes a powerful domain for sensing and for applications where ultra-low latency still matters.</div></div><div style="opacity:0" class="planet_info is-meo"><div>Medium Earth Orbit is the sweet spot. With dramatically fewer satellites,&nbsp;MEO&nbsp;provides true global reach while maintaining strong network performance. K2’s&nbsp;MEO&nbsp;systems unlock efficient, resilient, and scalable constellations, without the complexity of operating hundreds or thousands of&nbsp;LEO&nbsp;spacecraft</div><div class="planet_info-group"><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Temperature</div><div class="text-color-secondary">545Fº</div></div><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Deeper orbits are where</div><div class="text-color-secondary">coverage and comms become</div></div><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Distance from earth</div><div class="text-color-secondary">564.545.000 km</div></div><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Deeper orbits are where</div><div class="text-color-secondary">coverage and comms become</div></div></div></div><div style="opacity:0" class="planet_info is-geo"><div>Geostationary orbit anchors the world’s most trusted broadcast and communications . Our&nbsp;GEO&nbsp;satellites deliver high power, long life, and continuous regional coverage, extending K2 capability all the way to 36,000 km.</div><div class="planet_info-group"><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Temperature</div><div class="text-color-secondary">545Fº</div></div><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Deeper orbits are where</div><div class="text-color-secondary">coverage and comms become</div></div><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Distance from earth</div><div class="text-color-secondary">564.545.000 km</div></div><div class="planet_info-item"><div>Deeper orbits a